{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-frobenius-self-pairing-chirality","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:frobenius-self-pairing-chirality","kind":"definition","title":"Frobenius self-pairing chirality factor $a_K(\\beta) = \\tau(\\beta\\beta^{\\ast})/\\tau(1)$","cites":["references/jones1987"],"tags":["chirality","frobenius","self-pairing","antipode","categorical"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor","text":"frobenius-self-pairing-chirality.md","leanSource":"frobenius-self-pairing-chirality.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:frobenius-self-pairing-chirality\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(A, \\tau)</code> be a self-dual Frobenius algebra and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta \\in A</code> a braid word. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta^*</code> denote the image of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta</code> under the algebra antipode. The <strong>chirality factor</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta</code> is the normalized Frobenius norm:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  a_K(\\beta)\n  \\;:=\\;\n  \\frac{\\tau(\\beta \\cdot \\beta^*)}{\\tau(1 \\cdot 1)}.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-self-pairing-chirality.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.24.1","page":"b/def-frobenius-self-pairing-chirality","qa":{"counts":{"pass":79,"fail":0,"warn":2,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":64},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-self-pairing-chirality.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
